  "releaseNotes": "* Breaking: the package no longer depends on CommunityToolkit.Mvvm; an app that uses the toolkit adds the package itself\n                        * Breaking: DayTappedMessage is removed; use DayTappedCommand to react to taps\n                        * Added TimeProvider: tells the calendar which day is today, so tests and screenshots can pin it\n                        * Added DayViewHeight: the height of the day cells, while DayViewSize stays their width, so a DayViewTemplate can list the events of a day in a month grid\n                        * Added observed day collections: a day of the EventCollection stored as an ObservableCollection<T> updates its cell and the event list when its events change (#20)\n                        * Added runtime SwipeDetectionDisabled: it can be changed at any time\n                        * Fix: the arrows and swipes stay within MinimumDate and MaximumDate, and the year arrows raise MonthChanged\n                        * Fix: week numbers are counted from FirstDayOfWeek, and cultures with a non-Gregorian calendar show Gregorian month names and years\n                        * Fix: crashes with ShownDate set to default(DateTime), near the ends of DateTime, with Events or Culture set to null, and in Native AOT apps when the footer was shown\n                        * Fix: on Android a swipe that starts on a day changes the month\n                        * Fix: a calendar whose handler is replaced by another one keeps handling day taps and changes of Events (#270)\n                        * Updated MAUI to version 10.0.130\n                        * The full list is in CHANGELOG.md",
